# Dependencies and Tooling

## Workspace configuration (M-CARGO-WORKSPACE)
- Edition, `rust-version`, `publish = false`, lints and dependency versions are set once in the root
  `Cargo.toml` and inherited: `edition.workspace = true`, `[lints] workspace = true`,
  `serde = { workspace = true }`.
- Crates never declare their own lint tables or dependency versions.
- The canonical lint block lives in `.cursor/skills/scaffolding-rust-crate/templates.md`; change it only
  via a `chore(lints)` commit.
- Toolchain is pinned in `rust-toolchain.toml` to an exact stable version with `rustfmt` and `clippy`.

## Lint overrides
- Use `#[expect(lint, reason = "…")]`, not `#[allow]` (M-LINT-OVERRIDE-EXPECT). `allow` without a reason is denied.
- Scope overrides to the smallest item. Crate-wide overrides need an ADR.

## Adding or updating a dependency (AGENTS.md rule 14)
Ask before adding. Each new crate must have:
- [ ] A concrete need that std or an existing dependency cannot meet;
- [ ] Active maintenance, reasonable download/usage, no unresolved RUSTSEC advisories;
- [ ] A license compatible with the distribution model **pending LEGAL-001** — permissive (MIT, Apache-2.0,
      BSD, ISC, Zlib, Unicode) is pre-cleared; anything copyleft, PHP-licensed, or unknown is blocked until
      legal review;
- [ ] Minimal features (`default-features = false` where practical);
- [ ] No bundled Zend Engine, libphp, or PHP binary — ever (master plan §0.1).

Prefer well-established crates for infrastructure (e.g. `serde`, `thiserror`, `tracing`, `proptest`);
each still passes the checklist above.

## CI gate (every PR)
```bash
cargo fmt --all --check
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings
cargo test --workspace --all-features
RUSTDOCFLAGS="-D warnings" cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --all-features
cargo deny check            # advisories, licenses, bans, sources
```
Additional scheduled gates: `cargo hack --each-feature check` (features additive, M-FEATURES-ADDITIVE),
unused-dependency scan, Miri for unsafe-permitted crates, fuzz runs, forbidden-PHP-binary scan of images.

## Features
- Cargo features are additive and never change WordPress-observable behavior silently.
- Test-only code lives behind `test-util`; reference-oracle tooling never becomes a production feature.
